                                "sense_id": "27ce4178-16ce-3f60-8a7a-3b9c29a1d6c5",
                                "text": "For as it was with the Moraller Heathen they did the things contained in the Law, yet they were dead; so a people may doe the things contained in the Gospell too, and yet be dead […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b9a8a37-e2c4-4acf-a8e3-370fea83264d",
                                "sense_id": "27ce4178-16ce-3f60-8a7a-3b9c29a1d6c5",
                                "text": "Why what’s innocenter or moraller than a Punch and Judy?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "082d98f8-16fd-4443-90ce-3ee7b1f2a74b",
                                "sense_id": "27ce4178-16ce-3f60-8a7a-3b9c29a1d6c5",
                                "text": "1933, Helen de Guerry Simpson, The Woman on the Beast, Book II, France, 1789, (i),\n[…] we betake ourselves nightly to the Opera or Coliseum, and daily to the Palais Royal, where we walk under the trees, at all the moraller hours."
                            }
                        ]
